\begin{itemize}
    \item 1. Sample Preparation: Dissolve 1 g of Cs-137 (or 125 g of Cs-137-N) in 20 mL of 0.1 M NaClO₄ solution, add 1 mL of 1 N HClO₄, and filter through a 0.45 µM filter.
    \item 2. Measurement Setup: Place the NaClO₄ solution in a 250 mL polypropylene or glass ampoule. Secure the ampoule with a rubber stopper, insert the Cs-137 pellet, and insert a 1 cm diameter Au pellet into the pinhole. Seal the ampoule and headspace.
    \item 3. Cs-137 Detector: Set up a graphite-core detector (GCD) or scintillation counter using 25 mL scintillation fluid. Place the GCD at ±10 cm from the pellet.
\end{itemize}
